The server bundles presets.json, fields.json, preset_categories.json and the en and cs
translations of @openstreetmap/id-tagging-schema 7.3.0
(https://github.com/openstreetmap/id-tagging-schema), copied from node_modules at build time,
Copyright (c) iD Contributors, ISC License.

The map style reproduces iD's look (https://github.com/openstreetmap/iD), Copyright (c) 2017 iD
Contributors, ISC License; at build time the web app bundles from the @openstreetmap/id package its
icon sprites (dist/img/*-sprite.svg) and area fill patterns (dist/img/pattern/*.png), and ports iD's
line, area, vertex, pin and pattern styling rules.

The web app's editor chunk bundles iD's editing core (modules of @openstreetmap/id 2.42.3:
actions, behaviours, operations, validations, the graph and history, and its locale files),
Copyright (c) 2017 iD Contributors, ISC License (https://github.com/openstreetmap/iD).

The web app bundles MapLibre GL JS (https://github.com/maplibre/maplibre-gl-js), Copyright (c) 2023
MapLibre contributors, BSD-3-Clause License, and CodeMirror 6 (https://codemirror.net), Copyright (c)
Marijn Haverbeke and others, MIT License.

The web app bundles presets.min.json from id-tagging-schema
(https://github.com/openstreetmap/id-tagging-schema), Copyright (c) iD Contributors, ISC License, for
preset icon matching.

Icons in iD's sprites come from:
- Temaki (https://github.com/rapideditor/temaki), CC0 1.0
- Maki (https://github.com/mapbox/maki), CC0 1.0
- Pinhead (https://github.com/waysidemapping/pinhead), CC0 1.0
- Font Awesome Free (https://fontawesome.com), icons under CC BY 4.0
- Roentgen (https://github.com/enzet/Roentgen), CC BY 4.0

The web app bundles clipper2-ts (https://github.com/countertype/clipper2-ts), a TypeScript port of
Clipper2, Copyright (c) Angus Johnson 2010-2025, Boost Software License 1.0.

The rules tests include a GOL built from OpenStreetMap highways of Opava-Kateřinky
(rules/src/test/resources/fixtures/katerinky-highways.gol, also as web/src/editor/validation/fixtures/
katerinky-highways.osm.gz), © OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL.

The server bundles server/src/main/resources/replication/czech-republic.poly, the Czech Republic
extract polygon from Geofabrik (https://download.geofabrik.de/europe/czech-republic.poly), derived
from OpenStreetMap data, © OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL.

The server tests include six OpenStreetMap minutely replication diffs (sequences 7360200 to 7360205
of 2026-11-05, server/src/test/resources/replication/minute/) from
https://planet.openstreetmap.org/replication/minute/, with user names and uids removed,
© OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL.

